<node id="Spanish">
  <data key="d0">Spanish</data>
  <data key="d1">language</data>
  <data key="d2">Spanish is a widely-spoken Romance language with global influence. It originated on the Iberian Peninsula and has become the primary language of Spain and numerous countries in Latin America. With its rich cultural heritage and various dialects, Spanish is known for its linguistic diversity.

This language is featured prominently in the given context, serving multiple purposes. It is used for dialogue and narration, providing a means of communication and storytelling. Spanish is also employed in legal contexts, with certain terms translated into Quechua. For instance, the word 'violación' (meaning violation or rape) is a Spanish term adopted into Quechua. The language is further used to discuss marital status, offering distinct phrasing for men and women.

The versatility of Spanish is evident in its ability to adapt to different situations. It is often used as a second language or when Quechua is not understood. The language's vocabulary and expressions are translated for clarity, ensuring effective communication across different audiences.

In summary, Spanish, as presented in the descriptions, is a powerful language that facilitates communication, cultural understanding, and legal discourse. Its widespread use and adaptability make it an essential tool for various fields and regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Spanish is the language in which the examples are presented, and the question about marital status is phrased differently for men and women.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2359b63060bffecbf151abda4a0e00e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe0463a18dd608713c653a9219dd642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e466951a02859e9c19941a6374ec66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a55cc5abf7a5677430321b4d65fed09c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80c358465308937a6455c6e67461cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de05426836a86fb66736a747e092f16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0316609c53848e02f3ae95df7bf25b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-381b4d28ca48af9c962b80a582f83fd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b090bec40f9538cbb2debd0666e4bf32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55295324133559174ddb1bcbc3b46097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a7802ab519ce0d5da18765756fac50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d364753e678b22b3f4d135c76a8ab9fe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976892</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quechua">
  <data key="d0">Quechua</data>
  <data key="d1">language</data>
  <data key="d2">Quechua, a native South American language family, holds immense historical and cultural significance, particularly in the Andes region. It is widely spoken across various countries, including Peru, where its presence is especially notable in the Cusco area. Quechua boasts a rich linguistic tapestry, comprising numerous dialects and absorbing influences from other languages, notably Spanish.

This language family is characterized by its distinct vocabulary and unique linguistic features. For instance, the inclusion of numbers within textual representations and a specific variant with 18 consonants sets it apart. Quechua Cusco Collao is one such dialect, further emphasizing the language's diversity.

The language's adaptability is evident in its ability to incorporate elements from Spanish, especially in legal terminology. The word 'violación', derived from Spanish, is used in Quechua legal contexts. Quechua is actively employed in official settings, including courts and police interactions, and is essential for effective communication with the accused and some court personnel.

Quechua's cultural importance is deeply intertwined with its role in everyday dialogue, reflecting its status as a living, evolving language. The Cusco region, with its rich historical background, has significantly influenced the development of Quechua, contributing to its unique characteristics and dialectical diversity.

In summary, Quechua is a vibrant language family with a rich cultural heritage, serving as a vital communication tool in various official and everyday contexts, particularly in the South American region.&lt;SEP&gt;Quechua is a language spoken by indigenous people in South America, with various phrases and expressions used in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Quechua is an indigenous language family spoken in South America, primarily in the Andes region.&lt;SEP&gt;Quechua is the original language of some terms and expressions, requiring translation for a broader audience.&lt;SEP&gt;Quechua is a language with a variant that has 18 consonants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2359b63060bffecbf151abda4a0e00e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0b83dcddf2661f5ae9efb3440b98eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-903eae28c3678cd1170d8d47a488993c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe0463a18dd608713c653a9219dd642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a55cc5abf7a5677430321b4d65fed09c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-947fcfbc2e830e58af6390516b8c4432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878ee0410f5c542af0bcaf87e350c0c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80c358465308937a6455c6e67461cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5db0c89ce2e469022c73b77bda53c4dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de05426836a86fb66736a747e092f16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0316609c53848e02f3ae95df7bf25b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b090bec40f9538cbb2debd0666e4bf32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55295324133559174ddb1bcbc3b46097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a7802ab519ce0d5da18765756fac50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-371f25b818860b8f145cae0fde86b4d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2885b89726947656d89803f886c108ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5f151b10b61bfb94f36e9ed7cd9546</data>
