<node id="Maya">
  <data key="d0">Maya</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Maya is an individual with a multifaceted presence in the text. Primarily, Maya is involved in prostitution, as suggested by the term 'prostitutaru'. This connection is a significant aspect of Maya's characterisation.

Additionally, Maya is mentioned in the context of legal assistance, suggesting a potential legal issue or involvement with the justice system. This is further supported by the description of Maya's thoughts and actions, indicating that their perspective and behaviour are central to the narrative.

Maya's association with the territory or its governance implies a political or administrative role, or at least a connection to those in power. This multifaceted portrayal of Maya highlights their complex role and the various aspects of their life that are explored in the text. The combination of their involvement in prostitution, legal matters, and governance creates an intriguing character with a unique position in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Maya is a person involved in prostitution, as indicated by the term 'prostitutaru'.&lt;SEP&gt;Maya is a person in the text.</data>
