<node id="Family">
  <data key="d0">Family</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A document section concerning family matters.&lt;SEP&gt;Family is a legal entity that requires protection under public order due to its significance and role in ensuring the survival of its members.&lt;SEP&gt;The family is a social unit recognized as a natural and fundamental institution of society, receiving protection but to a lesser extent than other vulnerable groups.&lt;SEP&gt;The family is a legal entity of great importance, requiring protection under public order due to its dependence on financial support for basic survival needs such as food, clothing, housing, health, education, work training, and recreation.&lt;SEP&gt;Family is a social unit composed of individuals related by blood, marriage, or adoption, typically living together and sharing resources and responsibilities.</data>
