<node id="Violence">
  <data key="d0">Violence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Violence is a central theme, with the text emphasizing the importance of understanding its history and frequency.&lt;SEP&gt;Violence is a central issue in the woman's situation, causing fear and danger.&lt;SEP&gt;Violence is a recurring theme in the text, with a focus on violence against women in a family context.&lt;SEP&gt;Violence is a recurring theme in the text, manifesting in various forms, including physical, sexual, and psychological abuse.&lt;SEP&gt;Violence refers to the use of physical force with the intent to harm, damage, or abuse another person or property.&lt;SEP&gt;Violence is a recurring theme in the text, manifesting in various forms, including physical, sexual, and psychological abuse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1cf42a40dbb9b66b9afee3a75222b066&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-616c4afcd1863ac879f5d0babeaa7a64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fb20731e95d1532f2c1fbb9a4f42c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b735361c36ea047b824180ccbb100ba0</data>
