<node id="Geometric Shape">
  <data key="d0">Geometric Shape</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A geometric shape refers to a figure or form in geometry, characterized by its dimensions, angles, and properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A geometric shape is a shape that can be described mathematically, such as a circle, triangle, or square.&lt;SEP&gt;Geometric shape, known as 'forma geométrica' in Quechua Central, is a shape with specific geometric properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A two-dimensional figure or three-dimensional object with specific properties and characteristics, such as lines, angles, or surfaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e839c62082efb86813a5a27fd2dfc4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47093ee0a15bed613718c57d60752485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1ccfe4b83f56423b977d019c039df9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2328fbabe7e3d0414f8b5dd5fe2110a</data>
