<node id="Spouse">
  <data key="d0">Spouse</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Spouse is a term that refers to a partner in a marital relationship, commonly used to describe a husband or wife. The descriptions provided offer a complex and multifaceted view of this entity.

Firstly, the spouse is identified as a woman who has passed away, indicating a past marital relationship. This is contrasted by other descriptions that suggest a more contentious dynamic. The spouse is accused of being the perpetrator of violence, responsible for physical and emotional harm inflicted on their partner. This is further supported by another description detailing the spouse's alleged alcoholism, physical abuse, and financial neglect, as reported by a patient. 

In a different context, the spouse is described as a person legally entitled to a share of their partner's income, highlighting the financial aspects of marriage. Another description shifts the focus to the spouse's role as a parent, where they are connected to a question about the father's occupation. 

Furthermore, the spouse is mentioned as the spouse of an interrogated person, with a potential threat implied. This suggests a scenario where the spouse's role is one of suspicion or concern. 

In summary, the descriptions of 'Spouse' encompass various roles and situations, ranging from a deceased partner to an abuser, a legal beneficiary, a parent, and a potential threat. These diverse portrayals highlight the complexity of marital relationships and the varying circumstances that the term 'spouse' can encompass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44ae68371001162545d2e093c276a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f2c622027ead125c0ebec582c3c42f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff7bca4527b3e6238e521a5f546c3063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce5acde591b064cf26e9c2820db261ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1b2c9e7decea4bad65244951a79c736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d0de7afc8d73954eebbcc483bf0a6d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
