  <data key="d0">Llaqta</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Llaqta refers to a city or a town, with specific phrases indicating direction or location within the city or town.&lt;SEP&gt;Llaqta is a city, town, or village, as 'llaqta' means 'city, town, or village' in Quechua.&lt;SEP&gt;Llaqta refers to a city, town, or country, indicating a geographical location or political entity.&lt;SEP&gt;Llaqta is a person whose name appears in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Llaqta is a location mentioned in the text, possibly a city or town.&lt;SEP&gt;Llaqta is a Quechua word for 'town' or 'city'.&lt;SEP&gt;Llaqta refers to a city or a town, with specific phrases indicating direction or location within the city or town.</data>
