  <data key="d0">Huchachasqa</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Huchachasqa is a person who is declared guilty or responsible, with 'huchachasqa' meaning 'declared guilty' or 'responsible' in Quechua.&lt;SEP&gt;Huchachasqa is the action of declaring someone guilty or responsible, with 'huchachasqa' being the Quechua word for 'to declare guilty'.&lt;SEP&gt;Huchachasqa is a guilty person, indicating someone who has committed a wrongdoing.&lt;SEP&gt;Huchachasqa is a person who is a party to a lawsuit, but their rights are not being defended by the Huchachakuq.&lt;SEP&gt;Huchachasqa is a proposed translation for the legal term "Sentencia."</data>
