<node id="Judicial Process">
  <data key="d0">Judicial Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The judicial process involves formal court procedures and hearings to determine legal matters related to child custody and visitation.&lt;SEP&gt;The judicial process involves taking legal matters to a court of law for resolution by a judge or jury.&lt;SEP&gt;The Judicial Process is a procedure initiated by a petition to judicial organs, aiming to secure a resolution based on arguments and motivation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Judicial Process refers to the legal proceedings, with a focus on initiating a lawsuit.&lt;SEP&gt;The judicial process involves stages of investigation and trial, with specific rules and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;The concept of a judicial process is introduced, suggesting a legal course of action.&lt;SEP&gt;The Judicial Process is a legal procedure referenced in the text as an alternative to conciliation for establishing a visitation regime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a10c47969bde293870692b12386abf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d64b4097269cba14bedfe5206349706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f034844fc671eb87fee070aaac310b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23814e870d18ae597a1ddc01fae433c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce161295dc1dc61553f279a1d37ee22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7dd5abcee0d5dcaa9b6abe1680f02f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a279353fdbac92b0d437e064bf224a94</data>
