<node id="Law">
  <data key="d0">Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Law refers to the system of rules and regulations established by a governing body to maintain order and resolve disputes.&lt;SEP&gt;Law refers to a set of rules and regulations established by a governing body, defining rights, responsibilities, and the conduct of individuals and entities.&lt;SEP&gt;Law refers to a system of rules and regulations governing a community or country.&lt;SEP&gt;The law sets the maximum percentage of earnings that can be garnished, ensuring a fair distribution of resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Law refers to the system of rules and regulations governing the validity and proof of legal acts.&lt;SEP&gt;Law refers to a system of rules and regulations governing a community or country.&lt;SEP&gt;Law refers to a set of rules and regulations established by a governing body, defining rights, responsibilities, and the conduct of individuals and entities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a10c47969bde293870692b12386abf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f471a51a8d056592a2c993e3ce2f35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5153b7114bbe81cf01bd129ebd30d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a63f3394bc76241522ba3047ffdf17b6</data>
