<node id="Lima">
  <data key="d0">Lima</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Lima, the capital city of Peru, is a significant location with various notable attributes. It is home to the Ministry of Education, also known as the Ministerio de Educación, which is responsible for overseeing educational institutions and policies within the country. The city's educational prominence is further highlighted by the presence of the Universidad de Lima, a prominent institution of higher learning.

Lima is also associated with a legal context, as a legal decision was made there on November 17, 2017, although the specifics of the case are not provided. Additionally, Lima is the city where the son of Damaso is pursuing his medical studies, indicating a focus on education and professional development.

Furthermore, Lima has a connection to academia and research. The cited authors of REYNA ALFARO's text are affiliated with the city, suggesting a scholarly environment and intellectual contributions. This multifaceted description of Lima highlights its role as an administrative, educational, and legal hub in Peru, with a diverse range of associations and activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Lima is a city where a legal decision was made in a case involving psychological violence.&lt;SEP&gt;Lima is a city where the Colegio de Abogados and the Llank'ana Wasi Apaqninkuna are located.&lt;SEP&gt;Lima is a department within the political organization of Peru.&lt;SEP&gt;Lima is a city in Peru, where the Universidad de Lima is located.</data>
