<node id="Visitation Regime">
  <data key="d0">Visitation Regime</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The visitation regime is a legal framework that governs the right of parents and children to maintain contact, communication, and visitation, especially when they do not live together.&lt;SEP&gt;Visitation regime refers to the structured arrangement for parents to spend time with their children, which can be established through mediation or court processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Visitation Regime is a legal arrangement that can be established through conciliation or judicial means, ensuring the right of a parent to visit their child.&lt;SEP&gt;Visitation regime refers to the structured arrangement for parents to spend time with their children, which can be established through mediation or court processes.</data>
