</node>
<node id="Autoridad">
  <data key="d0">Autoridad</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoridad refers to the power or right to make decisions, enforce rules, or command obedience within a given context, such as political or institutional authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoridad refers to authority or the power to make decisions and enforce rules.&lt;SEP&gt;The Autoridad is a governing body with the authority to prohibit certain actions for reasons of public security or health.&lt;SEP&gt;A person in a position of authority, such as a judge, public official, or law enforcement officer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0705140ff04e29bafa317684eb08b87e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e508f9708ed96caa69c30bb37feadd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a9301293978372e472233b60af9887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e0d319bfebf641ea9d83c13b11b66b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783974853</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Propiedad">
  <data key="d0">Propiedad</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Propiedad refers to the legal right of ownership over tangible or intangible assets, such as land, buildings, intellectual property, or other resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Propiedad is a mathematical term for a property, translated as "kapuy" in Quechua.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0705140ff04e29bafa317684eb08b87e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-533dcc7ad2776c9bf8f55e7b6a1fe007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783972108</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol consumption is a factor in the context of violence, with the spouse's drunkenness influencing their aggressive behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol consumption is a factor in the context of violence, with the spouse's drunkenness influencing their aggressive behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Abuse">
  <data key="d0">Physical Abuse</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical abuse is a form of violence where the victim experiences bodily harm, including being slapped, punched, kicked, and dragged.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical abuse is a form of violence where the victim experiences bodily harm, including being slapped, punched, kicked, and dragged.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Psychological Abuse">
  <data key="d0">Psychological Abuse</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Psychological abuse involves verbal and emotional attacks, such as insults, humiliation, and controlling behavior, which are directed towards the victim by their spouse.&lt;SEP&gt;Psychological abuse involves verbal and emotional attacks, such as insults, humiliation, and controlling behavior, which are directed towards the victim by their spouse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Financial Dependence">
  <data key="d0">Financial Dependence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Financial dependence is a situation where the victim relies on their spouse for financial support, which can hinder their ability to leave an abusive relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial dependence is a situation where the victim relies on their spouse for financial support, which can hinder their ability to leave an abusive relationship.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emotional Dependence">
  <data key="d0">Emotional Dependence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Emotional dependence is a state where the victim has a strong emotional attachment to their abuser, hoping for change and an end to the violence.&lt;SEP&gt;Emotional dependence is a state where the victim has a strong emotional attachment to their abuser, hoping for change and an end to the violence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Promises">
  <data key="d0">Promises</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Promises are made by the spouse to the victim, assuring them that the violence will stop or that they will change, which may lead to the victim staying in the abusive relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;Promises are made by the spouse to the victim, assuring them that the violence will stop or that they will change, which may lead to the victim staying in the abusive relationship.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sexual Violence">
  <data key="d0">Sexual Violence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sexual violence is a form of abuse where the spouse forces the victim to engage in sexual acts against their will.&lt;SEP&gt;Sexual violence is a form of abuse where the spouse forces the victim to engage in sexual acts against their will.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Denial">
  <data key="d0">Denial</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Denial is a strategy employed by the victim, where they may have chosen not to report the violence or seek help earlier, possibly due to promises made by the spouse or a belief that the violence would not recur.&lt;SEP&gt;Denial is a strategy employed by the victim, where they may have chosen not to report the violence or seek help earlier, possibly due to promises made by the spouse or a belief that the violence would not recur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Questionnaire">
  <data key="d0">Questionnaire</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The questionnaire is a structured set of questions designed to gather information about the victim's experience of violence and the dynamics of their relationship with the abuser.&lt;SEP&gt;The questionnaire is a structured set of questions designed to gather information about the victim's experience of violence and the dynamics of their relationship with the abuser.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Questionnaire Sections">
  <data key="d0">Questionnaire Sections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The questionnaire is divided into sections, each focusing on a specific aspect of the violence and the victim's experience, including physical abuse, sexual violence, psychological abuse, and the victim's reasons for tolerating the abuse.&lt;SEP&gt;The questionnaire is divided into sections, each focusing on a specific aspect of the violence and the victim's experience, including physical abuse, sexual violence, psychological abuse, and the victim's reasons for tolerating the abuse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e8a16c78b13a67457341724148b39f0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
