<node id="Alimentos">
  <data key="d0">Alimentos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alimentos is a multifaceted term with legal and conceptual significance. In legal contexts, Alimentos primarily pertains to family law, specifically addressing the obligation of providing support and sustenance. It is a legal process and term used to describe the provision of financial assistance to ensure the fulfillment of basic needs, particularly for children and family members. This support is comprehensive, covering various aspects of life, including education, health, housing, and even recreation.

The term originates from the concept of sustenance, which goes beyond mere physical needs. Alimentos encompasses both material and spiritual aspects of support. In this context, it involves meeting the essential requirements for a dignified life, such as housing, clothing, education, medical care, and psychological well-being. This broader interpretation aligns with the idea of ensuring children's rights and overall well-being.

Within the legal framework, Alimentos is often associated with alimony or child support. It is a subsection of family law that outlines the responsibilities of parents or guardians to provide for their children's needs. This legal obligation is comprehensive, ensuring that children are not only physically provided for but also receive the necessary support for their overall development and well-being.&lt;SEP&gt;Alimentos refers to the legal concept of providing sustenance and support, particularly within the context of family law.&lt;SEP&gt;Alimentos refers to the concept of sustenance, encompassing both material and spiritual aspects, as defined in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23076d917b5f16ee7eab9b311cf1c3bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c201256346c6e8f8c2fe9afe44af20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fa586f1c761d07237556ddd2413a79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51b698b915327cdd4e7a202791944718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13134384351e880b2431198d223451fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1df6f6222656abe631b0f2df6aafaf86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48eb5d0d3944ca1c839ca9284f462db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568aca3000572a2d41ada0786698b6bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0afa2cdd77fb81053ae8e35465c22abe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976645</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Código de los Niños y Adolescentes">
  <data key="d0">Código de los Niños y Adolescentes</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">The Código de los Niños y Adolescentes is a legal document related to children and adolescents, addressing public policies, social services, and legislative and administrative measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Código de los Niños y Adolescentes is a legal code mentioned in the context of protecting children's rights, including the right to alimentos.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código de los Niños y Adolescentes is a set of policies and regulations aimed at protecting and promoting the rights of children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código de los Niños y Adolescentes is a legal code that grants visitation rights to the non-custodial parent, as per Article 88.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código de los Niños y Adolescentes is a set of policies and regulations aimed at protecting and promoting the rights of children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código de los Niños y Adolescentes is a legal code that grants visitation rights to the non-custodial parent, as per Article 88.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51b698b915327cdd4e7a202791944718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ac4bcb0bf2854fe209cdf14a69c8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4e50b2a515a9cb5b8f74fc143a95d4e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artículo 3.4">
  <data key="d0">Artículo 3.4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Artículo 3.4 outlines the commitment of States Parties to implement all necessary administrative, legislative, and other measures to ensure the rights recognized in the Convention, particularly economic, social, and cultural rights, utilizing available resources and international cooperation when needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783969813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artículo 472 CC">
  <data key="d0">Artículo 472 CC</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Artículo 472 CC defines the concept of 'alimentos' in the context of national law, detailing essential provisions for sustenance, housing, clothing, education, training, medical and psychological assistance, and recreation, as well as pregnancy-related expenses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783969813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artículo 6 CNA">
  <data key="d0">Artículo 6 CNA</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Artículo 6 CNA emphasizes the duty and right of parents to provide food, education, and security to their children, while children have the duty to respect and assist their parents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783969813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Código Civil">
  <data key="d0">Código Civil</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">The Código Civil is a legal code that, along with the Código de los Niños y Adolescentes, forms part of the administrative and legislative measures implemented by States Parties to ensure the rights recognized in the Convention.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código Civil is a legal code that prescribes that only one parent will have custody.&lt;SEP&gt;Código Civil is a legal code mentioned as part of the legal framework for guaranteeing the right to alimentos.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código Civil is the civil code of a country, containing laws and regulations related to civil matters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código Civil is a legal code that prescribes the custody arrangement for children, stating that only one parent is responsible for custody.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código Civil is a legal code that prescribes parental custody arrangements, stating that only one parent will have custody.&lt;SEP&gt;The Código Civil is a legal code that prescribes the custody arrangement for children, stating that only one parent is responsible for custody.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d900365798801616ccdf1ba57e101cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51b698b915327cdd4e7a202791944718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c41555f6b1e63737c4c742bcd62c6783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d80cc2eeef6ca2518edabac4f237f40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4e50b2a515a9cb5b8f74fc143a95d4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1942b13571e8da57f121f5097003b921</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Varsi">
  <data key="d0">Varsi</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Varsi is a prominent legal scholar and author, widely cited in the field of family law. Varsi's expertise lies in the intricate web of legal relationships within families, particularly concerning patrimonial aspects and economic obligations. Their work is referenced to understand the natural law perspective on the duty of parents to provide for their offspring, shedding light on the legal intricacies of familial responsibilities.

One of Varsi's notable contributions is a treatise on family law, published in 2012. This comprehensive work delves into the criteria for determining alimony, offering valuable insights into the economic relationships within families. The treatise has become a go-to reference for scholars and legal professionals, as evidenced by its citations in various texts, including a specific mention on page 451.

Varsi's writings provide a unique perspective on the legal aspects of familial duties, especially regarding food obligations and the broader economic dynamics within families. Their work is instrumental in shaping the understanding of family law, offering a nuanced exploration of the legal responsibilities and relationships that underpin family structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54eb792fbb06b16a5d980e148b1557af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51b698b915327cdd4e7a202791944718&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d23b0244bc4d9b9364a43c6c4e69e8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28ef892595b005185f05fed2db135474&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0afa2cdd77fb81053ae8e35465c22abe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783976793</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="García">
  <data key="d0">García</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">García is a cited author who provides the Colombian doctrine's understanding of 'alimentos', including the obligation to cover pregnancy and childbirth expenses.&lt;SEP&gt;García is a cited source, providing information on the alimentante's economic considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;García is a source cited on page 110.&lt;SEP&gt;García is a legal scholar or author referenced in the text, providing insights on Mexican law and food obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;García is a cited source, providing information on the alimentante's economic considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;García is a source cited on page 110.</data>
