<node id="Article 3.4">
  <data key="d0">Article 3.4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 3.4 outlines the commitment of States Parties to implement all necessary administrative, legislative, and other measures to ensure the rights recognized in the Convention, particularly economic, social, and cultural rights, utilizing available resources and international cooperation when needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783969813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Article 472 CC">
  <data key="d0">Article 472 CC</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 472 CC defines the concept of 'alimentos' in the context of national law, detailing essential provisions for sustenance, housing, clothing, education, training, medical and psychological assistance, and recreation, as well as pregnancy-related expenses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783969813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Article 6 CNA">
  <data key="d0">Article 6 CNA</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 6 CNA emphasizes the duty and right of parents to provide food, education, and security to their children, while children have the duty to respect and assist their parents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1512cd85e4ab6988d2546f436ad1f350</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783969813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
