  <data key="d2">Alimony is a legal obligation to provide financial support to a former spouse or partner, ensuring their basic needs are met.&lt;SEP&gt;Alimony is a legal obligation for one spouse to provide financial support to the other after a divorce or separation, ensuring the recipient's maintenance.&lt;SEP&gt;Alimony is a legal obligation for one party to financially support another, typically in the context of divorce or separation.&lt;SEP&gt;Alimony refers to the legal obligation to provide financial support to a family member or former spouse.&lt;SEP&gt;Alimony is a legal obligation for one party to financially support another, typically in the context of divorce or separation.</data>
