</node>
<node id="Child's Right to Adequate Standard of Living">
  <data key="d0">Child's Right to Adequate Standard of Living</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The child's right to an adequate standard of living is a legal principle recognized by the Convention, ensuring the child's physical, mental, spiritual, moral, and social development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba9ec333aebf1f09df2b4159280bbd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971700</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adolescent">
  <data key="d0">Adolescent</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An adolescent is an individual in a stage of life between childhood and adulthood, considered a vulnerable group and entitled to protection and assistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba9ec333aebf1f09df2b4159280bbd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971700</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Child's Right to Food">
  <data key="d0">Child's Right to Food</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The child's right to food is a legal principle recognized by the Convention, ensuring that children receive the necessary conditions for their development from parents or other caregivers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba9ec333aebf1f09df2b4159280bbd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971700</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Child's Right to Protection">
  <data key="d0">Child's Right to Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The child's right to protection is a legal principle that ensures children receive the necessary care and protection for their well-being, taking into account the rights and responsibilities of parents, guardians, and other legal representatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba9ec333aebf1f09df2b4159280bbd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971700</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Child's Interest">
  <data key="d0">Child's Interest</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The child's interest is a legal principle that prioritizes the best interests of the child in all actions and decisions concerning them.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba9ec333aebf1f09df2b4159280bbd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971700</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Child's Right to Care">
  <data key="d0">Child's Right to Care</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The child's right to care is a legal principle that ensures children receive the necessary care and protection for their well-being, with the state committing to provide legal and administrative measures to fulfill this right.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba9ec333aebf1f09df2b4159280bbd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971700</data>
