<node id="Pension">
  <data key="d0">Pension</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A pension is a regular payment made to someone, often as a form of retirement income or as a form of support.&lt;SEP&gt;Pension is a form of financial support provided to individuals, often after retirement, and can be a factor in income distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;A pension is a fixed sum paid regularly, typically after retirement or as compensation, and can be adjusted based on income changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A pension is a regular payment made to someone following their retirement or to a surviving spouse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff7bca4527b3e6238e521a5f546c3063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568aca3000572a2d41ada0786698b6bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d80cc2eeef6ca2518edabac4f237f40</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783973931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proration">
  <data key="d0">Proration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proration is the process of dividing something into proportional parts, ensuring a fair distribution among multiple parties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Article 481 of the Civil Code">
  <data key="d0">Article 481 of the Civil Code</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 481 of the Civil Code outlines the criteria for setting food pensions, considering the needs of the recipient and the means of the provider.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Link">
  <data key="d0">Legal Link</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal link is a recognized relationship between individuals or entities, such as spouses, partners, or children, that forms the basis for food obligations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spouses">
  <data key="d0">Spouses</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Spouses are individuals who are legally married to each other and have a legal link for food purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Spouses are referenced in the context of their mutual obligation to provide support to each other.&lt;SEP&gt;Spouses are obligated to provide alimony to each other, and this obligation is based on the principle of family solidarity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9e969af4c3467565b30ab2cc8e1f611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064be7b670f607c7ad1909fcbe93be8d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783973960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cohabiting Partners">
  <data key="d0">Cohabiting Partners</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cohabiting partners are individuals who live together in a romantic relationship without being legally married, and they have a legal link for food.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Relationship">
  <data key="d0">Blood Relationship</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A blood relationship is a biological connection between individuals, such as the relationship between parents and children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Fiction">
  <data key="d0">Legal Fiction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal fiction is a concept or relationship that is recognized by law but does not exist in reality, such as the legal link between spouses or partners.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Successors">
  <data key="d0">Successors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Successors are individuals who are entitled to inherit the property or rights of another person upon their death, such as children or spouses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Necessity of the Alimentist">
  <data key="d0">Necessity of the Alimentist</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The necessity of the alimentist refers to the alimentist's inability to meet their own needs, often due to age, disability, or unemployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spanish Doctrine">
  <data key="d0">Spanish Doctrine</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Spanish doctrine refers to a set of legal principles and interpretations within the Spanish legal system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Objective Perspective">
  <data key="d0">Objective Perspective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The objective perspective is a viewpoint that focuses on facts and evidence, considering the initial and final conditions of a situation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exigibility">
  <data key="d0">Exigibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exigibility is the state of being enforceable or demandable, such as the obligation to provide food when needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initial Condition">
  <data key="d0">Initial Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The initial condition is the starting point or circumstance that triggers a legal obligation, such as the need for food.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Final Condition">
  <data key="d0">Final Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The final condition is the circumstance that brings a legal obligation to an end, such as when the alimentist no longer needs food for subsistence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783971948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quantification of Food">
  <data key="d0">Quantification of Food</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Quantification of food is the process of determining the amount of food to be provided, considering the needs of the recipient and the means of the provider.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c59dfd0a7722cdd48deb0ca97fc9d04</data>
