  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shared Custody">
  <data key="d0">Shared Custody</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Shared custody is a legal arrangement where both parents have equal time with their children, promoting parental involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Shared custody is a legal arrangement where both parents have equal rights and responsibilities for their child's care.&lt;SEP&gt;Shared custody, also known as co-parenting, is a legal concept originating from Anglo-Saxon law, allowing children to live with both parents despite separation, promoting their well-being and personality development.&lt;SEP&gt;Shared custody is a legal arrangement where both parents have equal rights and responsibilities for their child's care.&lt;SEP&gt;Shared custody is a legal arrangement where both parents have equal time with their children, promoting parental involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Shared custody, also known as co-parenting, is a legal concept originating from Anglo-Saxon law, allowing children to live with both parents despite separation, promoting their well-being and personality development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d85b4899031c6f4035d82c3302be488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec207adb098a275b293f0a5127247bc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c7ef0e15dd05864adbc502c748046ce</data>
