<node id="Article 478 CC">
  <data key="d0">Article 478 CC</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 478 CC specifies the priority of maintenance obligations, stating that if a spouse is unable to provide maintenance without endangering their own subsistence, the obligation passes to other relatives before the spouse.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 478 CC outlines the conditions under which alimony obligations may shift from one spouse to the next in line.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 478 CC outlines the conditions under which alimony obligations may shift from one spouse to the next in line.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28ef892595b005185f05fed2db135474&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7c041e40623fc8901c57c019e099adf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
