</node>
<node id="Article 149 of the Criminal Code">
  <data key="d0">Article 149 of the Criminal Code</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 149 of the Criminal Code pertains to the crime of omission of family assistance, detailing penalties for non-compliance with court-ordered support obligations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127ae8b943be9ce7ac7a6f1a927830aa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783974351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Article 149 of the Peruvian Criminal Code">
  <data key="d0">Article 149 of the Peruvian Criminal Code</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 149 of the Peruvian Criminal Code outlines the crime of omission of family assistance, specifying punishments for various scenarios of non-compliance with court-ordered support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127ae8b943be9ce7ac7a6f1a927830aa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783974351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initial Paragraph">
  <data key="d0">Initial Paragraph</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The initial paragraph of Article 149 addresses the general punishment for failing to fulfill court-ordered support obligations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127ae8b943be9ce7ac7a6f1a927830aa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783974351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Second Paragraph">
  <data key="d0">Second Paragraph</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The second paragraph discusses increased penalties for specific circumstances of non-compliance, such as simulating another support obligation or maliciously quitting work.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127ae8b943be9ce7ac7a6f1a927830aa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783974351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Third Paragraph">
  <data key="d0">Third Paragraph</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The third paragraph outlines even harsher penalties for cases where the omission results in serious injury or death that could have been foreseen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127ae8b943be9ce7ac7a6f1a927830aa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1783974351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
